From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rvwasm <rvwasm@localhost>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:50:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] wasm: ucontext_t in the kernel's layout

musl had { uc_link; uc_sigmask; uc_stack; uc_mcontext; }, the kernel writes
asm-generic's { uc_flags; uc_link; uc_stack; uc_mcontext; uc_sigmask; }. A
handler that read uc_mcontext or uc_stack got garbage, a signal it added to
uc_sigmask was not blocked afterwards, and what it wrote into its idea of
uc_sigmask landed on the kernel's uc_stack, which rt_sigreturn passes to
restore_altstack() (a bad value there makes the sigreturn fail with SIGSEGV).
mcontext_t already matches struct sigcontext. (ABI: programs that use
ucontext_t need compiling again.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/wasm/bits/signal.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/wasm/bits/signal.h b/arch/wasm/bits/signal.h
index ab24d3d..ceeaab3 100644
--- a/arch/wasm/bits/signal.h
+++ b/arch/wasm/bits/signal.h
@@ -29,11 +29,13 @@ struct sigaltstack {
 	size_t ss_size;
 };
 
+/* As the kernel writes it (asm-generic/ucontext.h): the signal mask last. */
 typedef struct __ucontext {
+	unsigned long uc_flags;
 	struct __ucontext *uc_link;
-	sigset_t uc_sigmask;
 	stack_t uc_stack;
 	mcontext_t uc_mcontext;
+	sigset_t uc_sigmask;
 } ucontext_t;
 
 #define SA_NOCLDSTOP  1
